LISPTC LANGUAGE

Common-Lisp-like dialect. (f a b) calls f with evaluated a and b. Only top-level
parenthesised forms are code; text around them is prose, ignored.
This reference and lang memories authoritative: name in none does not exist.
nil = () = empty list = ONLY false value. 0, "" and empty structures true. t
canonical true.

Special forms: quote, progn, cond, setq, lambda, macro, quasiquote, try.
Prelude macros: if, when, unless, and, or, let, let*, letrec, while, dolist,
dotimes, case, defun, defmacro, setf, push, pop, incf, decf, block,
return-from, catch, unwind-protect.
